  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through Monday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Rain and snow showers will persist across \nNortheastern Nevada through this afternoon. Valley snow will be \nshort-lived, however a Winter Weather Advisory is in effect for the \nRuby Mountains and East Humboldt Range due to the expectation of 5 \nto 10 inches in higher elevations. The storm system will exit to the \neast and showers will clear from west to east this evening, leaving \ndry conditions by nightfall. High temperatures will be in the 40s to \nmid 50s for today, warming into the 60s and 70s by Friday as a \ntransient upper high enters the area. Lows will be unseasonably cold \nthe next few nights, dropping to around 20 tonight. Vulnerable \nplants and plumbing should be protected if they haven't already been \nwinterized. There are some early indications of another cold and wet \nsystem to start next week, but details are few and far between this \nfar out.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence in rain and snow \nshowers today. Moderate confidence in dry and warming conditions \nstarting Wednesday. No changes were made to NBM output.",
